expenses. Net cash provided by operating activities reflects our net income adjusted for non-cash items, including non-cash operating
lease expense, depreciation, deferred tax expenses, fees for consulting services, loss on termination of right-of-use assets &#8211; finance
lease, allowance for credit loss, and changes in working capital items including accounts receivable, prepaid expense, deposits and other
receivable, accounts payable, retention receivable, accruals and other current liabilities, contract liabilities, income taxes payable
and lease liabilities &#8211; operating leases.</span></p>

